    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Luni River is the largest river in the Thar Desert region. It is brackish (saline) below Balotra. It flows in a south-westerly direction and ultimately drains into the Rann of Kutch. The Luni Basin covers about 37,000 sq km.",
      "id": "4fzq0gl"
    },
    {
      "id": "z6zvkkh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3.1.3 Internal Drainage Rivers"
    },
    {
      "id": "1aqf3i3",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Ghaggar River: Flows from Punjab, enters Rajasthan near Tibi (Hanumangarh) and disappears in desert near Suratgarh/Anupgarh. Also known as Drishadvati in ancient times.",
        "Kantli River: Flows through Jhunjhunu, also disappears in the desert.",
        "Sahibi (Ruparail): Originates near Jaipur region, drains into internal basins."
      ]
    },
