    {
      "id": "47r72x3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.4 Indira Gandhi Nahar Pariyojana (IGNP)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Indira Gandhi Canal (originally Rajasthan Canal) is the largest irrigation project in India. It originates from Harike Barrage in Punjab and brings water from the Sutlej-Beas river system to the Thar Desert.",
      "id": "cx3k4oc"
    },
